{
  /*
   * Type-checks every Common test file as one program: `npm run
   * compile-tests`, run by the compile-common job in the Compile workflow.
   *
   * Common's jest config transpiles only (ts-jest isolatedModules), the way
   * App's does, so the Common Test workflow does not type-check anything.
   * This is where that happens instead: once per commit, rather than once per
   * jest worker per import graph, which is what used to dominate every Common
   * Test shard.
   *
   * The build config (./tsconfig.json) excludes Tests so `npm run compile`
   * stays self-contained; everything else - paths, strictness, types - is
   * inherited, so a test is held to the same rules as the code it tests.
   * Common's global declaration files are listed as well: the build picks
   * them up through its default include, and this project would otherwise
   * only see what the tests import.
   *
   * Tests/tsconfig.json extends this file unchanged. Editors and ESLint's
   * typed linting (projectService in eslint.config.js) give each file the
   * nearest tsconfig.json that includes it, and without that file the nearest
   * for a Common test was the repository-root tsconfig.json - no "include",
   * so a program of the whole monorepo. Scripts/Lint/LintByProject.js lints
   * this program in an ESLint process of its own; `eslint .` in one process,
   * which also holds every other program, ran out of memory with it.
   */
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": [
    "Tests/**/*.ts",
    "Tests/**/*.tsx",
    "Typings/**/*.d.ts",
    "UI/index.d.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "build"]
}
